\par\par \b \uc2 RBNZ battles  \highlight22\uc2 Japan FX \highlight\uc2  day-traders post- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eric Burroughs   \par \uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2007\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 12 (Reuters) - New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces a tough opponent after having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday to weaken the high-flying New Zealand dollar: Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders eager to buy the high-yielding "kiwi" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Japanese day traders and other individual traders nearly doubled their bets on a stronger New Zealand dollar on Monday after the selling by the Reserve Bank of New Zealand in its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the NZ dollar was allowed to trade freely in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 Data from the Tokyo Financial Exchange showed that Japanese margin traders -- who use borrowed funds to boost the size of their bets -- raised their positions in the New Zealand dollar to $347 million from $180 million the previous day.   \par \par \uc2 While the positions at the TFX are not large relative to the overall market, analysts said they typify the trading style of Japanese investors: selling higher-yielding foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when they strike peaks against the yen, but then buying when they tumble.   \par \par \uc2 "Japanese retail investors were not discouraged by the authority's action," said Masafumi Yamamoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nikko  \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in Tokyo. "It is likely that Japanese retail investors will continue to increase their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure, especially that of high yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like NZD."   \par \par \uc2 The NZ dollar rose nearly half a percent to 91.65 yen <NZDJPY=R> on Tuesday, up from Monday's low near 90.80 yen but off the 17-year high near 93.00 yen struck late last week. The kiwi has steadily risen over the past seven years against the yen, more than doubling in value from its lows in late 2000.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  margin trading has boomed in the past few years as individuals look for ways to make money in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Financial Futures Association of Japan, which tracks \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  margin activity, estimates that trading volume surged to 109.2 trillion yen ($898.2 billion) in the January-March quarter, up 40 percent from the previous quarter.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese investors have flocked to online \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading and mutual funds featuring foreign assets for better returns, with short-term domestic rates still just 0.5 percent compared with New Zealand's 8 percent or 5.25 percent in the United States.   \par \par \uc2 Such Japanese demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assets has helped to spur the carry trade, in which the low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is used by investors as a cheap source of funds to buy higher-yielding assts.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand authorities have previously tried to tackle the Japanese hunger for their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially uridashi bonds denominated in the New Zealand dollar and sold directly to Japanese households.   \par \par \uc2 Officials from New Zealand's Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  visited banks and securities houses in Tokyo about a year and a half ago, saying investors needed to be warned of the risks of a potential sharp fall in the NZ dollar.   \par \par \uc2 But Japanese investors have been undeterred, and the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains among the most popular for uridashi bonds. ($1=121.58 Yen)   \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-NZDOLLAR/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|NAT|J|AUF|ND|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070612e36c000ph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
