\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Yen Weaker As Market Ignores G7 Warnings  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick Bennett  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 1,099 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2007\par 08:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The yen weakened against the dollar and dropped to a record low against the euro Monday after Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers failed to mention the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness in their final communique and made only cautionary remarks about carry trades.  \par \par \uc2 The lack of any specific warning, let alone action, on the yen at the G7 weekend meeting encouraged traders and investors to maintain and extend their bearish yen positions.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that further yen weakness is likely and would only be reversed by signals that the Bank of Japan will tighten monetary policy or some other shock that causes a shift in appetite for carry trades.  \par \par \uc2 The euro firmed modestly against the dollar, but remains within a broad consolidation range that has held for five-weeks.  \par \par \uc2 Trading activity was limited by a national holiday in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Japanese yen seems an extremely remote prospect," said Westpac \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists Robert Rennie and Sean Callow. "Hence for now, the G7 appears resigned to waiting and hoping the yen will turn gradually without policy action."  \par \par \uc2 The G7 communique didn't specifically mention the yen but had a slightly different description of Japan's economy from the previous communique and cautioned market participants to the risks that the yen could strengthen and Japanese interest rates rise as the Japanese recovery continues.  \par \par \uc2 But market participants didn't appear to take much notice of the warning.  \par \par \uc2 The "statement puts down the G7's marker on carry trades, but by itself is not enough to reverse the recent trend," said Morgan Stanley analysts Sophia Drossos and Sharon Yeshaya.  \par \par \uc2 At 0650 GMT the dollar was trading at Y121.94, below a four-year high of Y122.18 on Jan. 29, but up from Y121.80 late Friday in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was bid higher on buying by non-Japan investment houses, said a Singapore dealer. Stop loss buying is expected if the dollar trades above Y122.20.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.3027 up from $1.2992 in New York. Traders say that buying of euro against the dollar was primarily driven by demand for euro against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 But an overall positive outlook for the euro is also underpinned by more-hawkish-than-expected comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet Thursday, and also by comments made Saturday by ECB board member Mario Draghi, who said there remain "serious" risks that Eurozone inflation could rise in the next few months.  \par \par \uc2 Despite calls from European finance officials ahead of the G7 meeting for a solid discussion on the weak yen, a lack of action at the meeting spurred a further rise in the euro against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 At 0650 GMT, the euro was trading at Y158.83, below a record high of Y159.00 set Monday, but up from Y158.25 in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "We expect further weakness in the yen, with the euro to reach Y160 now a realistic near term target," said Rennie and Callow.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      U.S. Retail Sales, Bernanke, Japan GDP In Focus \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants say their focus has switched to data due from the U.S. including the January retail sales report on Wednesday and from Japan the release of fourth-quarter gross domestic product data on Thursday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke is due to give two-days of testimony before the Senate Banking Committee Wednesday and the House Financial Services Committee on Thursday. Bernanke will address the U.S. economic outlook with traders most interested in any clues to future monetary policy moves.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With previous pricing for an eventual easing of U.S. monetary policy having been pushed into the second half of the year, expectations for steady policy will allow traders to focus on impetus from outside of the U.S. including, but not limited to, the Japanese GDP data.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The prospect of a strong Japanese GDP result may raise the prospect of a policy tightening by the BOJ at next weeks meeting,which may boost the yen temporarily, but will unlikely erode all interest in carry trades unless the BOJ signals a series of rate hikes to come.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones survey of forecasts centers on a 1.0% quarter-on-quarter rise in GDP against a 0.2% rise in the third quarter.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This should be enough for the BOJ to proceed with lifting rates next week, although it is doubtful the yen would get much of a positive boost," said UBS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Ashley Davies.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Australian dollar weakened following a quarterly statement on monetary policy from the Reserve Bank of Australia, which lowered its forecast for inflation, but still expects inflation to be in the upper-half of the target band over the next few years.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, analysts expect Australian interest rates will remain on hold, which means the Australian dollar will continue to enjoy an interest rate premium over many other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , limiting any fall in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trading in the Chinese yuan was unaffected by the G7 statement, despite a technical change in G7 language, which stressed the need for China to focus on the trade-weighted value of the yuan.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was last quoted at CNY7.7570, up from its closing level Friday of CNY7.7476.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 01:50 EDT / 0650 GMT \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              121.93-95  121.78-83  +0.12  122.09  121.80   +2.41 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.3024-29  1.2991-92  +0.25  1.3028  1.2987   -1.32 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.9548-52  1.9482-85  +0.34  1.9567  1.9481   -0.26 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.2474-76  1.2485-88  -0.09  1.2490  1.2469   +2.40 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.1736-41  1.1731-35  +0.04  1.1746  1.1732   +0.69 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.7747-52  0.7759-62  -0.15  0.7783  0.7730   -1.85 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.6856-59  0.6819-23  +0.54  0.6864  0.6822   -2.68 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Yen              158.82-84  158.23-28  +0.37  159.00  158.23   +1.06 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Patrick Bennett, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4035; patrick.bennett@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Iain McDonald [ 12-02-07 0701GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070212e32c00073\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
