\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Yen Jumps On G7 Speculation; May Rise More  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 1,101 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2007\par 07:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Speculation that European policy makers may push for a stronger yen sent the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broadly higher in Asia Thursday, and some traders say the rally is likely to continue.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar tumbled a full yen to Y120.37 on the EBS dealing platform. The euro also lost nearly one and a half yen, falling to Y156.09, while the British pound tumbled more than Y2 to Y236.38.  \par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  bearing higher interest rates than the Japanese unit, such as the Australian and New Zealand dollars, dropped against the yen as well  \par \par \uc2 European officials will seek a more forceful stance on yen weakness at a planned meeting in February of finance chiefs from the Group of Seven countries and these expectations are encouraging in an already yen-bullish market after a sharp rise in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's finance minister, Koji Omi, said early Thursday that he hadn't heard of any possible talks on the yen at the G7 meeting, which is scheduled for Feb. 9-10 in Essen.  \par \par \uc2 But traders say there is potential of more European verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so U.S. and European hedge funds are buying back the yen, an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  they started initially Wednesday against the Australian dollar and the British pound, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate movements seen recently may last for a while," said Masashi Kurabe, senior manager at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading department.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's recent revival is more likely a temporary thing rather than a turnaround in its broad downtrend, but "there are quite large amounts of (yen-short) positions in the market, so I feel that it could take some time for the adjustments to run their course," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar could fall below Y119.00 if more reasons to buy the Japanese unit - such as disappointing U.S. economic data - emerge, Kurabe said. Even if nothing new were to come out, "the dollar (still) has a chance of falling to Y119.50 through (position) adjustments." YES  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said that the yen would get a further boost if the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled hints of raising interest rates in February.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan policy board member Miyako Suda, who analysts say likely voted for a rate rise at last week's policy board meeting, told business leaders in southern Japan that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shouldn't hesitate to tighten credit when its board is confident in the economic and price outlook. But she later said to reporters that she is "sure whether we will hike rates in February."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 23:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              120.44-45  121.12-18  -0.56  121.21  120.38   +1.16 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.2962-66  1.2965-69  -0.02  1.2972  1.2953   -1.79 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.9670-75  1.9687-91  -0.09  1.9697  1.9657   +0.36 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.2474-77  1.2479-83  -0.04  1.2492  1.2471   +2.40 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.1778-84  1.1785-87  -0.06  1.1790  1.1778   +1.05 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.7797-02  0.7810-14  -0.17  0.7819  0.7785   -1.22 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.6998-08  0.6995-05  +0.04  0.7019  0.6981   -0.67 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Yen              156.13-17  157.07-11  -0.60  157.20  156.05   -0.66 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 25-01-07 0610GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In another sign of her displeasure about easy credit at home, Suda voiced concerns about the consequences of maintaining a low rate for a prolonged period of time. Such side effects include yen-carry trades, a popular investment strategy to exploit Japan's low rates to earn profits overseas.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The point that I would like to emphasize is ... if expectations for very low rates stayed for a long period, this would overstimulate financial and corporate activities," she said, referring to yen-carry trades. "This eventually would cause big swings in the economy and prices."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While Thursday's yen-buying could be traced to speculation surrounding the G7 gathering, few traders were convinced that Europe and Japan are ready to close ranks behind the falling yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I'm doubtful they'll take action anytime soon," including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Mamoru Arai, senior vice president of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  division at Mizuho Corporate Bank.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is a "manipulation" of exchange rates that European countries appear to abhor. Also, Japan may be reluctant to act before Europe because Tokyo likely owns fewer euros than dollars in its foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to sell for the yen, Tokyo traders said. Moreover, the U.S., the country with the biggest influence on Japanese economic policy, has been mum about the yen, they said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Unless the dollar tops Y125.00, the U.S. probably won't get serious" about the yen, said Akifumi Uchida, deputy general manager of marketing at Sumitomo Trust and Banking.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fact that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets in recent years also reduces the chance that any country could put enough pressure on Tokyo to bolster its home \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To be sure, there is speculation that the G7 chiefs may discuss the source of the yen's weakness during their talks; Japanese interest rates currently stand at 0.25% compared with the U.S.' 5.25% and Europe's 3.50%. Still, the odds of them publicly reaching any consensus may be low, they said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Even if someone blames Japan's low interest rates, Tokyo can defend its position by highlighting the fact that prices (of goods and services) remain very slow to rise here and that the country can't resort to fiscal policy" because of its huge public debt, Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ's Kurabe said. "It can say that the only way left to boost growth is monetary policy," he added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, G7 central bankers probably want to avoid setting a precedent of interfering with a country's interest rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  probably doesn't want others to meddle in its policy making," Mizuho's Arai said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Iain McDonald and Tomoko Hosaka [ 25-01-07 0735GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070125e31p00087\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
