\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan end-Dec foreign reserves dip to $895.320 bln  \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2007\par 00:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 11 (Reuters) - Japan's official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's second largest, stood at $895.320 billion at the end of December, slightly below the record high hit a month earlier, government data showed on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2  Japan's reserves edged off the end-November peak of $896.949 billion, pulled down by a decline in the prices of foreign bonds and a depreciation in the euro, which reduced the dollar value of the euro-denominated reserves, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told reporters.  \par \par \uc2  Those factors outweighed the impact of interest-rate income from foreign bond holdings, the official added.  \par \par \uc2  Still, Japan remains No. 2 among the world's holders of reserves after China, the first country whose reserves surpassed $1 trillion.  \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breakdown of Japan's external reserves is a state secret, but historical data on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has mostly taken the form of dollar buying, suggests that most of the hefty reserves are in dollars.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves ballooned after yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a record 20 trillion yen ($170 billion) in 2003 and a further 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004, which saw a government campaign to prevent a rapid rise in the yen from aggravating deflation and derailing a fragile export-driven recovery.  \par \par \uc2  Tokyo has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since then as the world's second-largest economy has been enjoying modest but healthy economic growth amid signs of breaking free from years of deflation.  \par \par \uc2  The reserves included $749.291 billion in securities and $125.305 billion in deposits. The rest includes IMF reserve positions, special drawing rights and gold.       \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070110e31a0023x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
