\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Japan's Watanabe gives pause to yen bulls  \b0\par\par\uc2 By David McMahon  \par \uc2 863 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2006\par 22:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 24 (Reuters) - To analysts arguing that the Japanese yen is massively undervalued across the board, think twice.  \par \par \uc2 That was the message some market watchers took away from a speech in New York on Monday from Hiroshi Watanabe, Japan's vice Finance Minister and spokesman for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe said he did not regard the yen's current value as too low and said the "real effective exchange rate" (REER), which measures the value of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against an inflation-adjusted basket of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its trading partners, could be a "misleading" gauge of the yen's value.  \par \par \uc2 The REER shows the yen is currently at its weakest in more than two decades, and is one piece of evidence commonly cited by analysts who see room for a large appreciation in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Swiss bank UBS wrote in a note to clients on Tuesday that Watanabe's comments were "detrimental" to the bank's bullish stance on the yen. Meanwhile, Citigroup said the comments helped support a view that the yen would remain weak for the time being.  \par \par \uc2 "Mr. Watanabe's comments are broadly consistent with our view that the yen will trade on the soft side in the near term," Jeffrey Young, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in New York for the bank wrote in a note to clients.  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe tempered his remarks by adding he did not see any reason for the yen's value to deteriorate further. He also played down the impact of yen carry trades, under which speculators such as hedge funds have been selling yen for higher yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Outstanding carry trades probably amounted to only "several trillion yen", Watanabe said, pointing out that this figure was dwarfed by the average daily traded volume in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which is approaching $3 trillion by some measures.  \par \par \uc2 MIXED SIGNALS  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe's comments came at a time when the yen is close to 10-month lows against the dollar, around 120 yen per greenback. The yen also hit record lows against the euro earlier in this month.  \par \par \uc2 Also on Monday, Japan's Finance Minister Koji Omi reiterated the ministry's standard refrain that it would monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates carefully, and take appropriate action as needed.  \par \par \uc2 Traders keep a close eye on the utterances of MOF officials, which have presaged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the past.  \par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since early 2004, when its Finance Ministry wrapped up a record-breaking 15-month stretch in which it sold 35 trillion yen, almost all to buy dollars.  \par \par \uc2 For now at least, analysts say there is little chance \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the opposite direction to prevent the yen from weakening further.  \par \par \uc2 A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helps boost the yen value of big Japanese exporters' overseas sales in the auto and electronics industries. It also helps keep upward pressure on the price of imports, aiding Japan in its long battle against deflation.  \par \par \uc2 In the near term at least, some analysts said Watanabe's comments were implicitly giving a green light for the market to have another attempt at breaking the 120 in dollar/yen level.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan seems to think that dollar/yen is not really all that out of whack with fundamentals right now," said Greg Anderson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro. "A rise above 120 probably wouldn't set off too many alarm bells."  \par \par \uc2 Although policymakers in Japan have largely kept quiet about the yen's steady decline, the drop in the yen has led policymakers in the euro zone, South Korea and New Zealand to express concern.  \par \par \uc2 The latest such call to fall on deaf ears was from New Zealand trade Minister Phil Goff, who was reported by Dow Jones on Monday as saying he expected the kiwi dollar to decline against the yen over time.  \par \par \uc2 "It's tough to buck a trend," said Robert Fullem, manager of corporate \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ in New York. "There's a continued outflow of money from Japan into high yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe offered some reasons for the yen's weakness on Monday, pointing out that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's steady series of rates rises was helping support the euro. Japan has the lowest rates in the developed world, at 0.25 percent.  \par \par \uc2 By some measures at least, the yen is unmistakeably weak. According to the Economist's "Big Mac index", the yen is by far the most undervalued of the developed world's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the cheapest McDonald's hamburgers.  \par \par \uc2 Hamburgers aside, many traders see little letup in the dollar's rise against the yen in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 "There is interest to send this thing above 120, but its just a matter of who's got the guts to go out and buy into it," said Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi UFJ's Fullem.  \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by David McMahon, editing by Clive McKeef, Reuters messaging: david.mcmahon.com@reuters.net; email: david.mcmahon@reuters.com, tel: 1-646-223-6233))  \par \par \uc2 BA-MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -WATANABE (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|J  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061027e2ao002ib\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
