\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar, Euro Fall In Wake Of BOJ Article  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 748 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2006\par 08:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell versus the yen in Asia Wednesday as players sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a newspaper report suggested that the Bank of Japan is concerned about the yen's recent weakness.  \par \par \uc2 But players remain bullish toward the U.S. unit against the yen, saying such indirect warnings by the BOJ aren't enough to turn around the yen's persistent downtrend stemming from Japan's low interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Some said that the dollar, which was changing hands at Y118.50 in the afternoon, could rise to top Y120.00 this week if the U.S. consumer price data due later in the global day come in stronger than expected.  \par \par \uc2 "Players are looking for good reasons to buy the dollar," said Hidenori Kato, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Societe Generale in Tokyo. Any CPI figures that exceed expectations "may set off a trend for the market to try Y120 within this week."  \par \par \uc2 Economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires expect the core U.S. consumer price index, which excludes volatile food and energy prices, rose 0.2% on month in September.  \par \par \uc2 But after the markets have repeatedly failed to lift the dollar above Y120.00 since last week, other traders were skeptical about the U.S. unit's upside potentials.  \par \par \uc2 Players "need a boost as strong as a statement from the Fed that implies it may raise its interest rates again," said Tsutomu Soma, foreign securities senior manager at Okasan Securities Co. Ltd. Without such support, the greenback may range below Y119.50 for the rest of the year, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in Asian trading hours, European and U.S. hedge funds sold the dollar on a Nihon Keizai Shimbun report that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is planning to reinforce its monitoring of yen-carry trades, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The article indicated that the BOJ is uncomfortable with an increasing popularity of those trades, which exploit Japan's low interest rates to earn higher returns elsewhere and are often blamed as a main culprit behind yen weakness.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options market, the report prompted investors to buy contracts to hedge against possible further declines in the dollar/yen rate, traders said. Volatilites implied by dollar/yen options rose as a result, they said. But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later pared much of its losses as speculators warmed back to the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the yen. A BOJ spokesman also told Dow Jones Newswires later that while the bank is "interested" in yen-carry trades, "it's not as if we have stepped up monitoring of any specific transactions or investors."  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the newspaper article probably means that Japanese central bankers are keen to know the volume of yen-carry trades worldwide but have no intention to halt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline.  \par \par \uc2 "Their worry is an unexpected and huge unwinding of that kind of position could cause a strong buying back of the yen," said Kikuko Takeda, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi UFJ. "If they were to say they were trying to monitor strongly, the market would react by buying the yen, which would be quite the opposite to their intentions."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              118.55-60  118.90-93  -0.29  118.77  118.40   +0.66 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.2548-49  1.2543-45  +0.04  1.2555  1.2532   +5.94 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.8717-22  1.8698-03  +0.10  1.8725  1.8696   +8.64 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.2672-75  1.2679-84  -0.06  1.2693  1.2672   -3.51 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.1396-99  1.1410-14  -0.12  1.1412  1.1394   -1.90 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.7541-46  0.7535-38  +0.08  0.7546  0.7524   +2.72 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.6624-34  0.6644-54  -0.30  0.6634  0.6610   -2.99 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Yen              148.76-81  149.13-18  -0.25  148.94  148.49   +6.59   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2936; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Tomoko Hosaka [ 18-10-06 0629GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061018e2ai000c4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
