\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Watanabe: N Korea Test Had Limited Impact On Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2006\par 08:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Japan Vice Finance Minister Hiroshi Watanabe said Thursday North Korea's claim on Monday it had carried out a nuclear test had limited impact on the Japanese yen, and urged greater flexibility by China in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe also said the value of the yen in relation to the euro reflects market fundamentals and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring the exchange rate. [ 12-10-06 0651GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 "We have already absorbed the impact from the North Korea incident in the last two days," Watanabe told reporters in a briefing. "The impact itself was very much limited."  \par \par \uc2 The yen has weakened slightly since Pyongyang said Monday it had tested a nuclear weapon. The yen was trading around Y119.35 to the U.S. dollar Thursday compared with about Y119.00 at the start of the week.  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe said that although the euro has been rising against the yen, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't seen the need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We don't see any reason to make any measures at this moment...We are going to closely monitor the market," Watanabe said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate should reflect the fundamentals" of each economy, he added.  \par \par \uc2 In calling for greater \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility from Beijing, Watanabe said China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy isn't consistent with its macroeconomic policy.  \par \par \uc2 "Our position among the G7 is to ask China to have more flexibility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Watanabe said. "More flexibility is needed for China, not only for trade but also for effective money-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also macroeconomic policy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "Currently, the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is somewhat not consistent with the other macroeconomic policy."  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe was in Hong Kong to market Japanese government bonds in the region.  \par \par \uc2 Another Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, Chikahisa Sumi, who is director of the debt-management policy division, said there was "favorable" foreign interest in the bonds.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jeffrey Ng and Yun-Hee Kim, Dow Jones Newswires; 852-2802-7002; jeffrey.ng@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Theresa Davidovitz and Andrew Bullard [ 12-10-06 0736GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020061012e2ac000ue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
