\par\par \b \uc2 Euro falls versus yen, traders cite Jiji report  \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2006\par 10:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 3 (Reuters) - The euro fell around half a yen to the day's lows of 149.61 yen <EURJPY=> on Wednesday as traders said markets were nervous following a report from Jiji news agency.  \par \par \uc2 The article cited market speculation over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen.  \par \par \uc2 Traders also said there were rumours the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was checking rates in euro/yen, but said this was probably an excuse to sell the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "It's a few weak longs getting taken out above 150, there was a crazy runmour the ECB had been checking rates, which I'm very dubious about," said a London-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 "Also Jiji news is running a story that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen but I think that's very unlikely."  \par \par \uc2 Markets have grown nervous about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the yen against the euro after recent policymaker comments on euro/yen's strength.  \par \par \uc2 "There's obviously been rhetoric that indicates potentially a little bit of concern over the levels of euro/yen but to suggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wrong," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at BTM-UFJ.  \par \par \uc2 "We're still in a situation where they are debating whehter deflation is over or not."  \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061003e2a3000h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\p