\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Yen trade-weighted index hits 21-year low in Sept  \b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2006\par 07:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 3 (Reuters) - The yen's trade-weighted value fell to its weakest level in 21 years in September, reflecting the broad-based slide in the low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors have shunned it for higher-yielding counterparts.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's yen index, after adjusting for the inflation rates of trading partners, fell to 101.3 in September, the lowest since September 1985, according to data published on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 That means the yen has tumbled to its worst since the Plaza Accord in September 1985, when the Group of Five nations at the time agreed to devalue the U.S. dollar against the yen and German mark to help reverse the gaping U.S. trade deficit back then. The yen's weakness on a trade-weighted basis has provided the export-driven economy with a powerful stimulus by making Japanese goods comparatively cheaper than those from competing countries.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's depreciation was one of the main factors that helped boost confidence among big Japanese manufacturers in the September tankan survey to a two-year high, despite worries of a sharp slowdown in the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 "The yen is at the moment extremely competitive, there's no doubt about it," said Hiroshi Shiraishi, an economist at Lehman Brothers Japan.  \par \par \uc2 European officials in particular have taken issue over the euro's rise to all-time highs above 150 to the yen <EURJPY=R>.  \par \par \uc2 After the Group of Seven meeting in Singapore last month, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet and Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki both said the yen should reflect Japan's recovery from deflation.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have also described the euro/yen's rise as "wild" and "volatile".  \par \par \uc2 The questions over European discomfort on the yen were enough to even stir market rumours on Tuesday that authorities could actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen.  \par \par \uc2 For years Japanese officials have sought through both words and massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from strengthening. While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  still makes comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it has stayed out of the market since March 2004.  \par \par \uc2 This year the British pound <GBPJPY=R> has scaled an eight-year high against the yen, the Canadian dollar <CADJPY=R> a 14-year high and the South Korean won a nine-year peak <JPYKRW=R>, mainly due to the ultra-low interest rates in Japan compared with elsewhere.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan raised interest rates for the first time in six years in July to 0.25 percent from zero.  \par \par \uc2 But that pales with the 5.25 percent short-term rates in the United States and 3.25 percent in the euro zone.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's real effective exchange rate in September leaves it some 20 percent below the average of the past decade and some 10 percent beneath the average on the BOJ data going back to 1970.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shed some 39 percent from the all-time high of 165.5 in April 1995 on the BOJ index.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-YEN (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|NAT|J|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061003e2a30007n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
