\par\par \b \uc2 MOF's Watanabe to stay as Japan  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  policy tsar  \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2006\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 21 (Reuters) - Japan's top financial diplomat, Hiroshi Watanabe, will stay in his post in a coming annual personnel reshuffle, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday, confirming market expectations.  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe, vice finance minister for international affairs, has been the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy tsar since July 2004 and the MOF announcement suggests there will be no major change in Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since Watanabe took up his post.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities sold a record 20 trillion yen ($171 billion) in 2003 and another 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004, fearing the yen's strength would hurt the economy. But they have not stepped into the market since.  \par \par \uc2 Hideto Fujii, head of the ministry's budget bureau, will replace Koichi Hosokawa as vice finance minister in charge of domestic issues.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry also said Naoyuki Shinohara will become head of the international bureau from his current position as the bureau's deputy, replacing Kiyoto Ido.  \par \par \uc2 The appointments are expected to be approved by the Cabinet and officially take place next Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, ministry sources told Reuters that Yoichi Nemoto would replace Masatsugu Asakawa next week as the director of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market division.  \par \par \uc2 Nemoto is currently the director of the regional financial cooperation division. In the new post, he would work closely with Watanabe to set Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-MOF|LANGEN|J|ABN|M|D|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060721e27l000vf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
