\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Tanigaki Says US Strong-Dlr Policy Intact  \b0\par\par\uc2 741 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2006\par 08:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Updates with background, additional quotes from Tanigaki.) \par  \par    By Leika Kihara \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OSAKA (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki Monday took the rare move of quoting his U.S. counterpart as saying that a strong dollar is in the U.S. interest, in an attempt to dispel speculation that Tokyo is under pressure from Washington to turn a blind eye to the rising yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "I frequently hold talks over the phone with Group of Seven finance ministers, and I usually don't comment on what I discuss with them," Tanigaki said in talks with business executives in the Kansai region of western Japan.  \par \par \uc2 "But I need to say that in the past week, (U.S. Treasury Secretary John) Snow has said that the value of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should basically move in a way reflecting economic fundamentals in an open and competitive market, and that the U.S. maintains its stance that a strong dollar is in the U.S. interest," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The remarks underscore Tokyo's concern over growing market views that the U.S. is quietly acquiescing in the dollar's slide and is pressuring \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the yen's gains.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that Snow had pressured Tokyo to keep quiet on the dollar's declines heightened after Dow Jones Newswires reported that Tanigaki and Snow held phone talks last week.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar tumbled to an eight-month low against the yen last week amid such speculation. The U.S. unit, which was above Y113 at the beginning of May, now stands around Y109.50.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki shrugged off suspicions of U.S. pressure, saying that there has been "inaccurate debate (in the market) based on speculation" over what happened last week.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese finance minister later said in a press conference that the two points he quoted Snow on weren't mentioned directly to him. Instead, they were what he understood as being Snow's "basic understanding on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," as indicated in his recent public remarks, Tanigaki said.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, including Tanigaki, have repeatedly declined to comment on whether the bilateral phone talks took place.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Hopes China Keeps Up Efforts For Flexible Yuan \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tanigaki, in the talks with business executives, reiterated that Tokyo sticks to the agreement among G7 finance leaders that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate moves should reflect economic fundamentals, and that rapid and disorderly moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market are undesirable.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The G7 agreement, as shown in a statement issued after a meeting of G7 finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors in Washington last month, is a "commonly shared view" in the world, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, he again refrained from making explicit warnings over recent yen rises, only saying in the press conference that Tokyo needs to "closely monitor" the impact a higher yen could have on the economy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the dollar's recent demise, Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities haven't warned it will take "appropriate action" in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if necessary - a phrase that was used frequently when Tokyo was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily to stem sharp yen rises in the 15 months until March 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tanigaki, meanwhile, called on China to keep up its efforts to manage the yuan more flexibly, even after the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  broke through the psychologically important resistance level of 8.00 to the U.S. dollar Monday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I won't comment on whether a certain \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level, including that of the Chinese yuan, is high or low," Tanigaki said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The change in China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  system last July has been large, but Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  under the new system has been "conservative," Tanigaki said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have been saying that Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility is desirable, and we continue to hope for further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a signal that Beijing will allow its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate more rapidly, China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday set a key trading benchmark for the yuan under the key 8.00 level to the dollar for the first time.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That led to the dollar trading as low as CNY7.9972 on the over-the-counter market early Monday, down from its closing level Friday of CNY8.0061 and the lowest level since China abandoned the yuan's peg to the dollar in July last year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale [ 15-05-06 0639GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060515e25f000dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
