\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits 1-year lows before Fed, yen rallies  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2006\par 03:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds fresh quotes)  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 10 (Reuters) - The dollar hit one-year lows against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday as investors speculated about a pause in U.S. rate rises, while talk of higher Japanese interest rates boosted the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve is widely expected to raise overnight rates by 25 basis points for the 16th straight time at its meeting on Wednesday, taking the key rate to 5 percent. But markets are nervous that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will indicate a pause in its two-year tightening campaign.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was also under pressure ahead of the release of a U.S. Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report, which markets speculate may name China as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.  \par \par \uc2 The yen hit an 8-month peak against the dollar and 6-week high against the euro and short-term Japanese government bond yields hit 7-year highs on speculation that the Bank of Japan could start raising overnight rates from near-zero levels as soon as June.  \par \par \uc2 Sources close to the Bank of Japan said on Wednesday the BOJ was likely to use stronger wording to describe the improving economic outlook in its monthly report next week.  \par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of nervousness and erratic moves in the markets," said Adam Baines, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citigroup.  \par \par \uc2 "The Fed meeting tonight will be the next concrete thing for the markets to focus on."  \par \par \uc2 By 1145 GMT, the euro was up a quarter percent on the day at $1.2781, off an earlier one-year high of $1.2804.  \par \par \uc2 The euro ticked down slightly after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council member Axel Weber told Bloomberg interest rates must rise by at least 25 basis points in the euro zone. Markets are speculating about more aggressive rate hikes.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit one-year lows against sterling, the Swiss franc and an index of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , before recovering slightly.  \par \par \uc2 RUNAWAY YEN  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was down more than half a percent against the yen at an 8-month low of 110.32, and the euro dropped a third of a percent against the yen to a 6-week low of 141.14.  \par \par \uc2 "In the last day or two, the market focus has shifted to the interest rate story in Tokyo, and that is reinforcing the weak dollar story," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at BOTM-UFJ.  \par \par \uc2 After the initial yen rally, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said he opposed sharp moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates and that a G7 statement on global imbalances last month did not allude to a need for the dollar to fall.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar needs to decline but \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Harvard economics professor Martin Feldstein told Japanese financial newspaper Nikkei on Wednesday. Markets see Feldstein as a possible successor to U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow.  \par \par \uc2 KIWI PLUNGES  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell 1.5 percent on the day to 22-month lows against the yen and dropped 1 percent on the dollar as investors unwound carry trades, which involve borrowing low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buying high-yielding assets.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling fell against the dollar and euro after the Bank of England lowered its growth profile in its quarterly inflation report. Sterling earlier rose after data showing the British March trade deficit narrowed sharply.  \par \par \uc2 TO NAME, OR NOT?  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Open Market Comittee is expected to make its interest rate decision around 1815 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The market was also waiting for the U.S. Treasury report on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices of the United States' trading partners, due at 2000 GMT, with particular interest focused on whether China would be named as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts speculated it would not be, partly to avoid ruffling efforts to curb Iran's nuclear ambitions, in which Beijing is seen as a key negotiator with Tehran.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan rose against the dollar on Wednesday ahead of the report.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 5)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060510e25a0002c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
