\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slumps to eight-month low against yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Eric Burroughs  \par \uc2 714 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2006\par 08:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 8 (Reuters) - The dollar slid nearly 1 percent on Monday and hit an eight-month low against the yen after a top U.S. Treasury official suggested that Japanese policymakers should refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Timothy Adams, the U.S. Treasury's undersecretary for international affairs, said at the Asia Development Bank's meeting last week that it was appropriate \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen strength since March 2004 but "we should all refrain" from commenting on exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 The remarks were seen as a signal Washington wants the dollar to weaken against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of countries with hefty trade surpluses, especially in Asia, as a way to help fix global imbalances. The dollar was also smarting from data on Friday showing that U.S. businesses added 138,000 jobs in April, well below forecasts for a gain of 200,000.  \par \par \uc2 The underwhelming figure further fueled expectations the Federal Reserve is near the finale of its two-year credit tightening campaign. Since June 2004, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lifted rates 15 straight times, driving the dollar's rally last year.  \par \par \uc2 "Last week's jobs data has helped to further deteriorate dollar sentiment," said Nobuaki Kubo, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  planning manager at Resona Bank.  \par \par \uc2 He added that some market participants were closing short yen positions ahead of the Fed's policy meeting on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed is expected to bump up rates to 5 percent, but a growing number of dealers expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to signal that the end to rising rates is likely around the corner.  \par \par \uc2 By 0555 GMT, the dollar was down about 0.85 percent at 111.60 yen <JPY=>, its weakest since mid-September last year.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shed 6 percent against the yen in just three weeks and is down about 5 percent for the year.  \par \par \uc2 The euro shed more than a yen from late New York levels on Friday to 142.15 yen <EURJPY=R>.  \par \par \uc2 But the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was steady around $1.2735 <EUR=>, just below a one-year peak of $1.2765 struck on Friday. The pound changed hands at $1.8615 <GBP=D4> after striking a one-year high of $1.8654 in early action.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese markets reopened on Monday after the country's Golden Week break that started last Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 MORE WEAKNESS?  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has tumbled in the past two weeks since the Group of Seven economic powers called for countries with trade surpluses to allow more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, singling out China and Asia.  \par \par \uc2 As the yen has rallied, Japanese officials have repeated that excessive volatility in exchange rates is undesirable and that they are keeping a close eye on the market. The yen is often traded as a proxy for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Monday that Japan's stance was unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 Masafumi Yamamoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nikko Citigroup, said Japanese officials would keep up their warnings but were unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the yen's broad weakness and the Bank of Japan's move toward raising short-term interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 The yen hit a 20-year low in April on a trade-weighted and inflation-adjusted basis, according to BOJ data.  \par \par \uc2 "There's no reason to justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Yamamoto said.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts say the dollar is poised to deepen the slide against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the U.S. Treasury names Beijing a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in its report on the exchange rate practices of trade partners this week. The Treasury has not specified the day of release.  \par \par \uc2 At the ADB meeting, China said it would push reform of the tightly managed yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but would not take orders from other countries.  \par \par \uc2 Investors have interpreted last month's G7 statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an implicit call for a dollar drop, even as officials have taken pains to correct such a reading.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, Hiroshi Watanabe, told Reuters on the sidelines of the ADB meeting that the Fed, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan all agree the G7 statement did not point to a dollar fall. ($1=112.03 yen) (Additional reporting by Naomi Tajitsu)  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slumps to eight-month low|LANGEN|GNN|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060508e258000en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
