\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Japan officials decline comment as yen gains 1 pct  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chisa Fujioka  \par \uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2006\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds new Tanigaki comment)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 8 (Reuters) - Japanese government officials refrained from talking down the yen as it gained 1 percent against the dollar on Monday, saying they would not comment on day-to-day market moves.  \par \par \uc2 Their statements came after U.S. Treasury Undersecretary for International Affairs Tim Adams, speaking to reporters on the sidelines of the Asian Development Bank's annual meeting in India on Thursday, said the appropriate stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is simply not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , verbally or otherwise.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki declined to comment on the rapidly rising yen on Monday, but he said Tokyo's stance remained unchanged and the government would act in markets as needed.  \par \par \uc2 "I will not comment on day-to-day movements," Tanigaki told Reuters when asked about the yen's recent rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Our basic stance is the same as always," he said, referring to Japan's stated position that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should reflect economic fundamentals and that excessive volatility in rates is undesirable.  \par \par \uc2 Asked specifically about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's position on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Adams' comments, he said: "It is unchanged."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar hit an eight-month low around 111.62 yen on Monday after Adams' comments.  \par \par \uc2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Shinzo Abe separately made similar remarks, adding that he would also refrain from commenting on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities aimed at stemming the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 "Regarding the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I should like to refrain from commenting on that," he said when asked by reporters.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since record bouts of yen selling in the 15 months to March 2004, during which period Japan spent some 35 trillion yen to try and rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Officials were worried that the yen's strengthening to 110 to the dollar from 120 during that time would risk tipping the deflation-plagued economy into a prolonged recession by hurting exporters' profits and the price competitiveness of Japanese goods abroad.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's economy has improved since then and the yen has fallen, and the government has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  though officials often repeat the basic stance that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will act appropriately if needed -- a phrase that markets take to be verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The latest fall in the dollar came after below-consensus U.S. job growth in April fuelled expectations that the Federal Reserve will soon wrap up a two-year credit tightening campaign.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed meets on Wednesday and is expected to raise rates to 5 percent but tweak its post-meeting statement to flag a pause.  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to raise rates in June and later in the year, while the Bank of Japan is expected to raise interest rates at least once by the end of the year from current levels around zero. (Additional reporting by Tamawa Kadoya)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-TANIGAKI (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060508e2580003j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
