\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Dollar Declines Broadly, Prompted By G10 Meeting -2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 591 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2006\par 11:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2006, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 May 08, 2006 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 Japan's interest rates have been at zero for a decade as the country has tackled persistent economic weakness and deflationary pressures.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui's comments come at a time when global interest rates are rising, though he also tempered his remarks by saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no set agenda for the timing of any interest rate tightening.  \par \par \uc2 Remarks made last week by Timothy Adams, U.S. Treasury undersecretary for international affairs, also encouraged dollar selling as traders took them to mean that Washington is raising pressure on Japan and other Asian nations to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen in order to curb protectionist sentiment at home and reduce the huge U.S. trade deficit.  \par \par \uc2 According to media reports, Adams told reporters at the Asian Development Bank's meeting in India that countries should refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as well as commenting on exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts had noted that given the recent moves in the dollar versus other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it is odd that the yen had failed to appreciate as much until Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Idea Global, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research firm in New York, suggested that there could be some catch up to be done in the dollar-yen pair given the gains in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Indeed, the U.S. dollar hit an overnight eight-and-a-half-year low against the Singapore dollar and an eight-year low against South Korea's won and Malaysia's ringgit.  \par \par \uc2 "The yen has moved into line with the movements that we have seen on dollar (versus) Asia (\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and majors and given the U.S. warnings for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," noted Divyang Shah, global strategist for Idea Global in London.  \par \par \uc2 Shah said that given the warning from the U.S. and the lack of comments thus far from BOJ officials, "yen longs remain attractive." Long positions are bets that a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to gain.  \par \par \uc2 And for the time being, the cards are stacked against the dollar, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "We suspect that the dollar will fall further because the pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to be huge," noted Steven Barrow, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London.  \par \par \uc2 "If the G7 is working hard to convince Asia (particularly China) to avoid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation, Japanese policy makers will hardly send the right message if they try to break the dollar's fall with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.  \par \par \uc2 With the dollar continuing to weaken, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's attention is now focused firmly on the upcoming Treasury \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  report due out this week. While the market seems divided about the major issue - whether China will be named a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator - most feel that no matter what the Treasury does, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will feel pressure in particular versus the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Also this week the Federal Reserve policy board will meet to make its interest rate decision, largely expected to lift short term rates by 25 basis points to 5.0%.  \par \par \uc2 Markets will closely scrutinize the accompanying statement in an attempt to divine Fed direction over the course of the next few meetings. The dollar has been under pressure even since Fed chief Ben Bernanke said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could pause its interest rate hike campaign.  \par \par \uc2 -By Azam Ahmed, Dow Jones Newswires, 201-938-2245; azam.ahmed@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Isabelle Lindenmayer, Corey Boles in Basel, and Takashi Nakamichi in Tokyo contributed to this report)  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 05-08-06 0945ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020060508e258001py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
