\par\par \b \uc2 Tanigaki: Japan should not tap  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  acct to cut debt  \b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 16 (Reuters) - Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki ruled out using part of retained earnings from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to help reduce the government's bulging debt on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The funds, held in the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Special Account (FEFSA), have been growing as Japan bought higher-yielding overseas assets, notably U.S. Treasuries, with virtually zero-cost funds raised in yen when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to contain the yen's rise.  \par \par \uc2 Although part of the earnings is transferred to the government's general budget each year, the rest is retained in the account over the years to cushion potential losses from overseas assets or from a rise in borrowing costs.  \par \par \uc2 "It is not appropriate to reduce the amount of the funds," Tanigaki told a parliamentary committee when asked about using the funds to help rein in Japan's swelling public debt, which at 150 percent of gross domestic product is the largest among major industrial nations.  \par \par \uc2 He said such a move could hurt the credibility of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy by fuelling speculation about Tokyo's ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 "Currently, there is a considerable gap between Japanese and U.S. interest rates that has boosted returns through the management of (foreign reserves), but we cannot hope that will continue indefinitely," Tanigaki said.  \par \par \uc2 "Unless we maintain a certain amount of those funds, people may start to have doubts about the sustainability of the special account or about its health. If so, market participants may speculate that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could no longer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that would hurt the function of the FEFSA," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The accumulated funds are expected to total about 15.1 trillion yen ($128.7 billion) at the end of fiscal 2006/07, which starts on April 1.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's largest at $850 billion at the end of February, have been yielding handsome profits due to high interest rates overseas.  \par \par \uc2 Three-month finance bills that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells to raise funds, for instance, are currently traded at 0.065 percent, while three-month U.S. Treasury bills trade at 4.5 percent.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for two years, but it sold a record-breaking 35 trillion yen during a 15-month stretch up to March 2004 -- more than the size of the entire Swiss economy.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki reiterated that the ministry would continue transferring a certain portion of retained earnings in the FEFSA to the general budget to help improve Japan's fiscal position.  \par \par \uc2 For fiscal 2006/07, 1.62 trillion yen will be transferred from the FEFSA, up from 1.42 trillion yen this fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 The transfer does not affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because the ministry in practice raises yen funds equivalent to its interest income on foreign bonds by issuing FBs and moves the proceeds to the general account, rather than repatriating the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets. ($1=117.34 Yen)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-TANIGAKI-ACCOUNT|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060316e23g001dj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
